 "MATH_0036": "$H = 0$", "MATH_0037": "$P = locally\\ finite\\ type$", "MATH_0038": "$C \\to A$", "MATH_0039": "$C \\to B$", "MATH_0040": "$B \\to B'$", "MATH_0041": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0042": "$C \\to B'$", "MATH_0043": "$P = locally\\ finite\\ presentation$", "MATH_0044": "$C \\to A$", "MATH_0045": "$C \\to B$", "MATH_0046": "$B \\to B'$", "MATH_0047": "$B \\to A$", "MATH_0048": "$A \\to B'$", "MATH_0049": "$C \\to B'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-compose-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-local-source-fppf-algebra}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-compose-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-flat-finitely-presented-permanence-algebra}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0007": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4b9bc2034157c6f0b2ff3ac4900414e2e939768055258015bf2ff097f93e00f4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:45132d071721f1befd882e4de9b7eff915ce3e18649ca3ad763abc35a5bbcc29", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an affine open and let\n<MATH_0002> be an affine open which maps into\n<MATH_0003>. The assumption on <MATH_0004> implies we can\nfind a standard affine fppf covering <MATH_0005>\nand lifts <MATH_0006>. Since <MATH_0007>\nis quasi-compact we can find finitely many affine opens\n<MATH_0008> lying over <MATH_0009>\nsuch that the image of each <MATH_0010>\nis contained in the union <MATH_0011>. Hence after\nreplacing each <MATH_0012> by a standard affine Zariski coverings\nof itself we may assume we have a\nstandard affine fppf covering <MATH_0013>\nsuch that each <MATH_0014> factors through an affine\nopen <MATH_0015> lying over <MATH_0016>.\nIn other words, we have ring maps <MATH_0017> for each <MATH_0018>.\nNote that we can also consider\n<MATH_0019>\nand that the ring map <MATH_0020> is faithfully flat and\nof finite presentation.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe case <MATH_0021>. In this case we know that <MATH_0022> is flat\nand we have to prove that <MATH_0023> is flat. Suppose that\n<MATH_0024> is an exact sequence of <MATH_0025>-modules. We want to\nshow that <MATH_0026>\nis exact. Let <MATH_0027> be its cohomology and let <MATH_0028> be the cohomology\nof <MATH_0029>. As\n<MATH_0030> is flat we know that <MATH_0031>. On the other hand\n<MATH_0032>\nis exact hence has zero cohomology. Hence the map\n<MATH_0033> is zero (as it factors through the zero module).\nThus <MATH_0034>. As <MATH_0035> is faithfully flat we conclude that\n<MATH_0036> as desired.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nThe case <MATH_0037>.\nIn this case we know that <MATH_0038> is of finite type and\nwe have to prove that <MATH_0039> is of finite type.\nBecause <MATH_0040> is of finite presentation (hence of finite type)\nwe see that <MATH_0041> is of finite type, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nTherefore <MATH_0042> is of finite type and we conclude by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nThe case <MATH_0043>.\nIn this case we know that <MATH_0044> is of finite presentation and\nwe have to prove that <MATH_0045> is of finite presentation.\nBecause <MATH_0046> is of finite presentation and <MATH_0047>\nof finite type we see that <MATH_0048> is of finite presentation, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nTherefore <MATH_0049> is of finite presentation and we conclude by\nLemma <REF_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0008>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2e89d66fb4aaf956bf456f639ef541d25218c28cd94bbe2610ac77ddf145e41f", "unit_id": "inventory:descent:06NB:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:descent:0347:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:3d367d80eb2b11fa2b6ecdfeb06ffc1c3c7d043b7218d50a273bd0a8ae4df579", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 174249, "byte_start": 173473, "file": "descent.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:afe7af9500391c6212df2323b7d27454b62ba0dbfa81fcebc1bf58f74b4b37fd", "line_end": 4632, "line_start": 4619}, "owner_tag": "0347", "parent_tag": "0347", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0347", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-reduced}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-section-descending-properties}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-variants}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{section-descent-finiteness-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e9adc384594ac6de2d12123a32663a7a3b959b4ef15fa0b3050b8e8726a578f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:33bf83d32c16a02b1dbfdade4346bd94dd71a427dae4d896d6e475df710fa932", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIt often happens one can prove the members of a covering of a scheme\nhave a certain property. In many cases this implies the scheme has the\nproperty too. For example, if <MATH_0001> is a scheme, and <MATH_0002>\nis a surjective flat morphism such that <MATH_0003> is a reduced scheme, then <MATH_0004> is\nreduced. You can prove this by looking at local rings and using\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe say that the property of being reduced\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>descends through flat surjective morphisms<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nSome results of this type are collected in\nAlgebra, Section <REF_0002> and\nfor schemes in Section <REF_0003>.\nSome analogous results on descending properties\nof morphisms are in Section <REF_0004>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:07fdd8c724157851f1056ccf9208d57186fa4d7792a1fee58